{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/768851-creating-a-pack-questions","id":768851,"title":"Creating a pack (Questions)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-18T19:05:09-08:00","id":768851,"title":"Creating a pack (Questions)","content":"Ok, so we start a new Werewolf The forsaken 2.0 game. <br /> It will be fun, Iknow it. I have a tons of ideas.<br /> <br /> However, something bugs me.<br /> <br /> The pack.<br /> <br /> I don't have my book right now since one of my friend do not know at all what kind of rules he is getting into, so I gave him my book for the week, to read and learn. However, the pack has change alot. Now we have Werewolves, Wolf Blood, and Humans in the pack.<br /> <br /> What ?!?<br /> <br /> Werewolves and Wolf bloods with tells. Cool, one of the wolf blood will have a tell that grants him a dog. It will be fun.<br /> <br /> But... How I'm I suppose to fit the humans in that ?<br /> <br /> Do the normal human know that there is some supernatural stuff, and dark evil things in the world ? Do they know about rituals, gifts, magic, and mystic weirdness found in the world of darkness ? They are friend... Ishould say brothers, with THEM !<br /> <br /> How do they fit, and what is the extent of their ability to cope with all those things that gravitates around a pack of werewolves !?!<br /> <br /> Can you explain to me, in a short way, the role of the humans in the pack ? It would help me alot. <br /> <br /> Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T19:21:27-08:00","id":768865,"title":"","content":"1) As a general rule, humans in the pack at least know a little something about what's up. They don't have to know everything, but they should know enough to help service the Totem and the needs of the pack. As a rule, they at least know about spirits. Really, the easier way to play this is to just bring them into knowledge full fold, but it's understandable if a lot of them go &quot;Look, tell me what I need to let you do your work and keep the rest to yourself.&quot; It's depends on how you want to handle it.<br /> <br /> It's worth noting that the default assumption of the World Of Darkness now is that everyone has some experience with the supernatural, at least one real encounter, if brief and hazy. It's just that most of humanity chooses to leave it at that and not push the issue. If they keep their head down and ignore the problem, the problem won't bother them...too much...hopefully. In their favor, they are right. Usually.<br /> <br /> 2) Humans can learn their own brand of magic, but the Uratha can't particularly help them in regards to that. Gifts and Rites have ties to the innate nature of the Wolves, and it's not something humans can replicate. Fetishes might work, and werewolves will probably run across some sort of resources to use if they want to arm their human brothers with magic. Not to mention that psychic characters are now readily available as options, with such merits being placed in with the rest of the merits in at least the GMC and WoD 2.0(this is based on an assumption).<br /> <br /> But, really, humans don't need magic, by and large because....<br /> <br /> 3)Werewolves very rarely let humanity take the charge. With Lunacy and the savagery of the Wolves running rampant, humans aren't the most resilient of folks.<br /> <br /> So, instead, packs rely on humans to round out the things they can or cannot do, the unglamorous jobs of faking identities or distracting cops or bumming around the slums, stuff like that. That's not to say they can't be on the field, but even then they prefer giving them distance with guns and stuff. Still, if you have enough humans and a cahalith to turns their fists into lethal, never say no to a swarm tactic if you think it'll work, or even better an absolute sucker punch-but all of that is risky. It's better to have them play the guy watching for trouble or setting the stage and let the wolf-blooded and werewolves handle the more upfront, hands-on stuff.<br /> <br /> So, in short, they act as support. Not strictly that, but mostly that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T19:30:22-08:00","id":768874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warriorshaman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/768851-creating-a-pack-questions#post768851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> However, the pack has change alot. Now we have Werewolves, Wolf Blood, and Humans in the pack.<br /> <br /> What ?!?<br /> <br /> Werewolves and Wolf bloods with tells. Cool, one of the wolf blood will have a tell that grants him a dog. It will be fun.<br /> <br /> But... How I'm I suppose to fit the humans in that ?<br /> <br /> Do the normal human know that there is some supernatural stuff, and dark evil things in the world ? Do they know about rituals, gifts, magic, and mystic weirdness found in the world of darkness ? They are friend... I should say brothers, with THEM !</div> </div> </div> </div>Think of the cult. Or better - biker gang. <i><b>Sons of Anarchy</b></i> are main inspiration for the <b>WtF</b> 2ED not without reasons. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> New Pack is in reality a cult of it's Totem, with Uratha being more of cult leaders, Wolf-Blooded are trusted servants/lineaments, and humans being every day member / normal bicker.<br /> <br /> Humans in Pack <b>do not</b>, normally, know what they are serving, really. They think that all the rituals made in the woods are typical hazing or similar non-spiritual ceremonies of the group the Pack is posing as. Or they really think they work for the &quot;ideological avatar&quot;, holy angel or any similar concept that do not point directly to the Spirit as their secret patron. Humans can even incante Totems Ban as some weird &quot;club motto&quot; in their ceremonies, without realizing they mark some sacred rule of the spirit guardian they serve.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warriorshaman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/768851-creating-a-pack-questions#post768851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do they fit, and what is the extent of their ability to cope with all those things that gravitates around a pack of werewolves !?!</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of humans <b>do not</b> Hunt with Uratha. They help &quot;leaders&quot; in the way they can - without going any near treats of Shadow. As the Oaths of Moon says: &quot;Herd must not know&quot;. Even if humans in Pack are 'family', they are distant and should not be exposed to the risk of <i>Hisil</i>.<br /> <br /> But humans <b>do know</b> they get bonuses for participating in Pack - some are stronger, some are wiser, quicker or just get fighting better. Those bonuses that Totem grants to Pack is granted to humans - they just suspect being in Pack is &quot;good for them&quot;. Like you are going to the new book club meetings and think &quot;damn, I learned soooo much by being there&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T19:54:32-08:00","id":768895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/768851-creating-a-pack-questions?p=768865#post768865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) As a general rule, humans in the pack at least know a little something about what's up. They don't have to know everything, but they should know enough to help service the Totem and the needs of the pack. As a rule, they at least know about spirits. Really, the easier way to play this is to just bring them into knowledge full fold, but it's understandable if a lot of them go &quot;Look, tell me what I need to let you do your work and keep the rest to yourself.&quot; It's depends on how you want to handle it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not agree with this - from mine reading of 2ED corebook it's more that humans know they serve <b><i>something</i></b>, and most of the time they think it's just some abstract figure, like collage fraternities in real world are swearing locality to Reason or Understanding, still thinking they are more mottos than real beings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/768851-creating-a-pack-questions?p=768865#post768865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth noting that the default assumption of the World Of Darkness now is that everyone has some experience with the supernatural, at least one real encounter, if brief and hazy. It's just that most of humanity chooses to leave it at that and not push the issue. If they keep their head down and ignore the problem, the problem won't bother them...too much...hopefully. In their favor, they are right. Usually.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the answer on the situation where Human Pack member sees Totem for what it is - I just think that 99% of them do not ever see this, thinking about Totem as more of the ideology behind the group, not literal lesser god they worship.<br /> <br /> Like all S<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sons_of_Anarchy_Motorcycle_Club\" target=\"_blank\">AMCRO would follow Reaper</a> ( the Spirit ) in WoD, <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/768851-creating-a-pack-questions?p=768865#post768865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Humans can learn their own brand of magic, but the Uratha can't particularly help them in regards to that. Gifts and Rites have ties to the innate nature of the Wolves, and it's not something humans can replicate. Fetishes might work, and werewolves will probably run across some sort of resources to use if they want to arm their human brothers with magic. Not to mention that psychic characters are now readily available as options, with such merits being placed in with the rest of the merits in at least the GMC and WoD 2.0(this is based on an assumption).</div> </div> </div> </div>Should not Pack Rites be usable by Humans also? On the way I pointed Hazaning and other similar non-spiritual ceremonies? Humans do not need to know they appesing gods of Shadow to make those sacrifices that need to be done, do they?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/768851-creating-a-pack-questions?p=768865#post768865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, instead, packs rely on humans to round out the things they can or cannot do, the unglamorous jobs of faking identities or distracting cops or bumming around the slums, stuff like that. That's not to say they can't be on the field, but even then they prefer giving them distance with guns and stuff. Still, if you have enough humans and a cahalith to turns their fists into lethal, never say no to a swarm tactic if you think it'll work, or even better an absolute sucker punch-but all of that is risky. It's better to have them play the guy watching for trouble or setting the stage and let the wolf-blooded and werewolves handle the more upfront, hands-on stuff.<br /> <br /> So, in short, they act as support. Not strictly that, but mostly that.</div> </div> </div> </div>They act as Bicker Gang. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=f5CUB96eV64\" data-code=\"f5CUB96eV64\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/f5CUB96eV64/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> And other example of Humans in Pack - German &quot;Werwolf Club&quot; and it's desendents. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HrMlpkIDVRE\" data-code=\"HrMlpkIDVRE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/HrMlpkIDVRE/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-18-2015, 11:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T21:40:41-08:00","id":768946,"title":"","content":"From the pack creation section:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Next, you create the humans who are in the pack, but aren\u2019t quite aware that they\u2019re in a formal pack, or that Uratha even exist. They\u2019re friends, family, coworkers, and other people who fall under the pack\u2019s auspices and protection. </div> </div> </div>Basically, anyone that's important to the Uratha of the pack can be considered pack members, even if they don't know there's even a pack to be a member of. Some may be fully in-the-know, others might believe they're part of a club or a gang but not be aware of its supernatural nature. Some may be aware of spirits but not of werewolves and believe they're in a cult that worships the Totem, others might have no idea and just think their family member hangs out with some strange people. What ever works for your pack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T21:41:32-08:00","id":768948,"title":"","content":"I'm with hamster on this one. My reading of it is that humans don't usually quite know what's going on, or what the pack is really up to. At least, more often than not.<br /> <br /> For example, one of the members of the pack in my current game is a homeless woman named Mrs. Hats who has helped the group numerous times. She doesn't even know she's in the pack but she is very loyal to them as they've developed a strong relationship over the years. She considers them a street gang more or less who care about the little people.<br /> <br /> nother human member is a med student who is roommates with one of the Uratha, he just considers the pack a group of close friends. Both these humans are just part of the outer circle of the group. On the periphery of what's going on but occasionally playing an important role supporting the pack.<br /> <br /> However, one human pack member is a police officer who got in over his head tracking a Claimed serial killer and was rescued by the pack. He does know a lot of what's going on and helps because the police can't fight monsters and he knows it. So there are degrees. Still, I think humans being a bit outside the loop is the norm as far as packs go. Wolfblooded tend to be a little further in, some still a bit outside it (assisting during rituals, helping gather info, etc), others being equal in status to their Uratha brethren.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T21:49:58-08:00","id":768954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warriorshaman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/768851-creating-a-pack-questions#post768851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But... How I'm I suppose to fit the humans in that ?<br /> <br /> Do the normal human know that there is some supernatural stuff, and dark evil things in the world ? Do they know about rituals, gifts, magic, and mystic weirdness found in the world of darkness ? They are friend... Ishould say brothers, with THEM !<br /> <br /> How do they fit, and what is the extent of their ability to cope with all those things that gravitates around a pack of werewolves !?!<br /> <br /> Can you explain to me, in a short way, the role of the humans in the pack ? It would help me alot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone's really covered what humans know. A big reason not to expose humans to werewolves is because they can be affected by Lunacy, which can grind away at their Integrity and get them killed.<br /> <br /> Humans are normally going to be people a werewolf member of the pack cares about or is involved with. A roommate who has access to a character's personal life, a family member who the werewolf wants to protect, valued employees who the werewolf views as theirs, a lover who can never really know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T23:40:21-08:00","id":769002,"title":"","content":"Can a normal human in the pack, but in the perifery be a psychic ? And who in the pack, outside of the Uratha themselves, take the Totem Merits ? And if the totem merit cannot be taken by the humans, wich could be totaly understandable, the question is, Do the totem care about them like he would do with the others ?<br /> <br /> Thanks for those answers guys. It does help alot !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T23:45:06-08:00","id":769004,"title":"","content":"If you are in the pack, you receive the totem benefit.<br /> <br /> I don't see how someone could be a psychic in the periphery, but a human packmate can be psychic.<br /> <br /> Considering spirits, vampires, changelings, and more can be packmates, there's not much in terms of limits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T05:13:35-08:00","id":769124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warriorshaman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/768851-creating-a-pack-questions?p=769002#post769002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a normal human in the pack, but in the perifery be a psychic ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And who in the pack, outside of the Uratha themselves, take the Totem Merits ? </div> </div> </div>Wolf-blooded and other supernaturals, like vampires or changelings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if the totem merit cannot be taken by the humans, wich could be totaly understandable, the question is, Do the totem care about them like he would do with the others ? </div> </div> </div>Every member of the werewolf's pack gains the Resonant Condition for the totem, allowing it to potentially access the material realm easier. In addition, although I don't believe it outright says this, I think it means Essence created by them is more palatable to the totem. Also there's a number of rites and gifts that allow packmates, including humans, to take a larger part in things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-19-2015, 08:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T06:37:36-08:00","id":769191,"title":"","content":"You can also have animal pack members. Wolves I think can join naturally, most others need to be brought in via one of the Nature facets. Makes it interesting if your totem grants a dot of intelligence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T06:58:51-08:00","id":769199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/768851-creating-a-pack-questions?p=769004#post769004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are in the pack, you receive the totem benefit.<br /> <br /> I don't see how someone could be a psychic in the periphery, but a human packmate can be psychic.<br /> <br /> Considering spirits, vampires, changelings, and more can be packmates, there's not much in terms of limits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if they invest in the totem in the first place, and even then, they don't need to know the ins and outs of that. After all, <i>The Herd Must Not Know.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T08:16:17-08:00","id":769267,"title":"","content":"No, totem benefits work on the entire pack, regardless of whether they have the merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T09:20:55-08:00","id":769325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warriorshaman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/768851-creating-a-pack-questions?p=769002#post769002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a normal human in the pack, but in the perifery be a psychic ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Pretty much anyone can be a member of a werewolf pack - humans, supernaturals, animals, spirits, you name it. It's rare for non-werewolves to be part of the hunting party, but even that isn't unheard of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warriorshaman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/768851-creating-a-pack-questions?p=769002#post769002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And who in the pack, outside of the Uratha themselves, take the Totem Merits ? And if the totem merit cannot be taken by the humans, wich could be totaly understandable, the question is, Do the totem care about them like he would do with the others ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Totem is a Werewolf-only Merit. Important Wolf-Blooded NPCs, such as those created with the Pack Creation rules, can buy up to one dot of Totem. Wolf-Blooded PCs can take the Pack Bond Merit, which allows them to buy a limited number of dots in Totem, at the cost of additional pack responsibilities. At one dot, they are respected members of the pack, at the same level as important NPCs as mentioned above, and can accordingly buy up to one dot in Totem. At three dots, they are full members of the hunting party and can buy up to five dots in Totem.<br /> <br /> Common house rules include ignoring the Wolf-Blooded only restriction on Pack Bond, ignoring the Werewolf-only restriction on Totem, and/or granting Pack Bond to important pack members for free.<br /> <br /> Pack Members that do not possess any dots in the Totem Merit do still recieve the benefits of the Totem's patronage, but do not get the bonus to rolls made to interac with the Totem that the Merit grants. Essentially, the Totem still recognizes these members as its own, but doesn't share as deep a bond with them as it does with those who have invested Merit dots into it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warriorshaman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/768851-creating-a-pack-questions?p=769002#post769002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for those answers guys. It does help alot !</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-19-2015, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 